    <briefdescription>
<para>An expression that converts the result of another expression to an Ecstasy Int, using the rules defined by <computeroutput><ref refid="d2/d58/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1constants_1_1_type_constant_1a6dd5153b5edbb566b3580a5cbcf15784" kindref="member">TypeConstant#isIntConvertible()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="d3/dba/classorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1_constant_1a05ba6849fb02513c325d81d21329994d" kindref="member">Constant#getIntValue()</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Steps, depending on the type of the underlying expression: <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Extract: For Bit, Nibble, Char, and Enum types, the Int value is extracted from the underlying expression, resulting in an Int type, so at this point the resulting type is IntNumber, regardless of the type of the underlying expression; </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Offset: The optional offset is applied to the IntNumber; </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Convert: If the IntNumber is not an Int, then the IntNumber.toInt() method is applied. </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
